     <script>
       const faqs = [
         {
           question: "Why do cats purr?",
           answer:
             "Cats often purr when they feel content, but they can also purr to self-soothe when stressed or healing. The vibration may help them stay calm and conserve energy."
         },
         {
           question: "Why do cats knead blankets and laps?",
           answer:
             "Kneading starts in kittenhood while nursing and often stays as a comfort behavior. Adult cats may knead when they feel safe, relaxed, and especially attached to a favorite person or cozy spot."
         },
         {
           question: "How much sleep do cats usually need?",
           answer:
             "Most adult cats sleep around 12 to 16 hours a day, and kittens or seniors can sleep even more. Their rest pattern comes from being natural crepuscular hunters, most active around dawn and dusk."
         },
         {
           question: "Do indoor cats still need playtime?",
           answer:
             "Yes. Indoor cats need daily play and enrichment to exercise their bodies and minds. Wand toys, climbing spaces, scratching posts, and food puzzles help prevent boredom and support healthy behavior."
         },
         {
           question: "Why do cats flick their tails?",
           answer:
             "Tail movement is part of cat body language. A relaxed upright tail can signal confidence, while fast flicking may mean excitement, irritation, or focused attention depending on the rest of the cat's posture."
         }
       ];

       const createId = (index) => `faq-panel-${index}`;

       function FAQItem({ question, answer, index }) {
         const panelId = createId(index);
         const buttonId = `faq-button-${index}`;

         return `
           <div class="example">
             <h2>
               <button
                 class="question-button"
                 id="${buttonId}"
                 type="button"
                 aria-expanded="false"
                 aria-controls="${panelId}"
               >
                 <span class="question-text">${question}</span>
                 <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
               </button>
             </h2>
             <div
               class="details"
               id="${panelId}"
               role="region"
